  "worked_solution": "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{270}^{\u2218}}$ by an angle of ${270}^{\u2218}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{270}^{\u2218}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{270}^{\u2218}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{\u2032}$ are $(0,0),(0,-2),(2,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
